    "body": "**Problem:** The four-argument `CBloomFilter` constructor is currently used only by unit tests and the fuzz target - which need it to exercise the sizing calculations directly.\r\nFor zero elements, the hash-function formula divides by zero and a zero false-positive rate makes the size formula convert `0 * log(0)` from `NaN` to `unsigned int`.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Construct the existing empty-filter state when the element count is zero, before evaluating either sizing formula.\r\nThe unit test catches the invalid `vData` floating-point calculation, and the fuzz target maps zero elements to a zero false-positive rate so an empty input lets UBSan reproduce each defect when its corresponding guard is removed.\r\n",
